     "md": "A **fertile** soil has plenty of **humus** (from rotted plants and animals), the right amount of water and air, and **minerals**. Earthworms and other small animals help to mix the soil. Farming without care can make the soil **poor**: crops use up minerals and rain washes away the top soil."
