    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Weather and climate",
     "md": "**Weather** changes from hour to hour. **Climate** is the average weather over many years. By recording the weather every day at the same time, pupils can find the **mean temperature**, the **total rainfall** and the **most common type of weather**. A table or graph makes the pattern easy to see."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Putting the thermometer in the Sun.\n- Reading the rain gauge while it is tilted.\n- Saying that one rainy day is a rainy climate.\n- Forgetting the units: °C and mm."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "From the graph: what was the highest temperature and at what time?",
     "steps": [
      "Find the highest point of the line: 31 °C.",
